    "The closed category list from 002_products.sql, named in all six languages.",
    "",
    "WHY THESE ARE ATTACHED TO EVERY PRODUCT. A category name is a search term. A",
    "person who types 'detergent' or 'lactate' or 'Getränke' is not naming a",
    "product, they are naming a shelf, and they still expect the dropdown to fill.",
    "So the seed importer writes each category's six names onto every product in",
    "it, as aliases of type 'category', which puts them in the product's search",
    "blob (S16).",
    "",
    "THE COST, WHICH IS REAL. 'lactate' now matches all fifteen dairy products",
    "equally, and popularity alone decides their order. That is the right answer",
    "for a shelf query and the wrong one for a product query, which is why the",
    "ranking in 004 scores an exact name match far above a blob match rather than",
    "treating them as the same evidence. Widening reach and ordering results are",
    "two different jobs; this file only does the first.",
    "",
    "Adding a category here is not enough on its own -- the check constraint in",
    "002_products.sql is the authority on which values exist, and the two lists",
    "have to be changed together."
